## Rules
1. Implement behaviour from the spec descriptions. Never special-case test inputs or return
   hardcoded/example data; tests use varied inputs and read data back.
2. Persist data with SQLAlchemy in SQLite via `app.db`. No in-memory globals for state.
3. Responses must validate against the spec schemas. Timestamps are timezone-aware (UTC);
   SQLite drops tzinfo, so re-attach UTC when reading.
4. Missing resources: raise `fastapi.HTTPException(status_code=404, detail="...")`.
5. Validation errors (422) come from the Pydantic models in `app.models`; do not weaken them.
6. Forbidden: `eval`, `exec`, `subprocess`, `os.system`, `importlib`, skipping tests,
   `# type: ignore` spam, network calls. Writes outside your allowed paths are rejected.
7. Code must pass: `ruff check`, `mypy --strict` (app/), `bandit`, `pytest`, and Schemathesis
   contract tests against the running server.
